@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Managing Environments with Azure DevOps";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Managing environments in Azure DevOps allows organizations to separate and control different stages of deployment, such as Development, Testing, Staging, and Production.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why Manage Environments?</h2>
        <p>In software development, different environments are required to ensure **reliability, scalability, and compliance** before releasing changes to production.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Isolates **development, testing, and production environments**.</li>
            <li>Ensures **consistent and controlled deployments**.</li>
            <li>Facilitates **approvals and security policies** for different environments.</li>
            <li>Enables **environment-specific configurations and variables**.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/environments.png" alt="Managing Environments in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Environment-based deployments in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Common Environments</h4>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Development:</strong> Used for testing new features and code changes.</li>
                <li><strong>Testing:</strong> QA and automated testing before production.</li>
                <li><strong>Staging:</strong> A pre-production environment to mimic the production setup.</li>
                <li><strong>Production:</strong> The live environment where end-users interact with the application.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Step-by-Step: Managing Environments in Azure DevOps</h2>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Create an Environment:</strong> Go to Azure DevOps > Pipelines > Environments and add a new environment.</li>
            <li><strong>Define Environment-Specific Variables:</strong> Configure settings like connection strings, resource names, and feature flags.</li>
            <li><strong>Set Up Deployment Approvals:</strong> Enforce approvals before moving to higher environments (Staging/Production).</li>
            <li><strong>Configure CI/CD Pipelines:</strong> Use environment-based conditions in pipelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor & Audit:</strong> Use logs and tracking to ensure deployments are secure.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Example YAML for Multi-Environment Deployment</h4>
            <pre>
stages:
- stage: Development
  jobs:
  - job: DeployDev
    steps:
    - script: echo "Deploying to Development"

- stage: Staging
  jobs:
  - job: DeployStaging
    steps:
    - script: echo "Deploying to Staging"
    - task: ManualValidation@0
      inputs:
        notifyUsers: 'user@example.com'
        instructions: 'Review and approve deployment to production'

- stage: Production
  jobs:
  - job: DeployProduction
    steps:
    - script: echo "Deploying to Production"
            </pre>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/ci-cd-environments.png" alt="CI/CD with Environments" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Managing CI/CD deployments across environments</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for Managing Environments</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use **separate environments** for development, testing, and production.</li>
            <li>Apply **role-based access control (RBAC)** to limit who can deploy.</li>
            <li>Define **environment-specific configurations** (e.g., API keys, secrets).</li>
            <li>Enable **approval processes** for sensitive environments.</li>
            <li>Monitor deployments using **Azure Monitor & Application Insights**.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Managing environments in Azure DevOps ensures **controlled and reliable software deployments** across different stages. By properly configuring environments, teams can enforce security, improve efficiency, and reduce deployment risks.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Azure Artifacts & Dependency Management** to manage and distribute software packages effectively.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-start mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("CreateResourcesAzureDevOps", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Creating Resources with Azure DevOps</a>
    </div>
</div>
